WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:01.877
♪♪

00:00:01.877 --> 00:00:04.463
Nick Mohammed:
I remember Jason, before we
filmed season two, said

00:00:04.755 --> 00:00:07.883
"it opens and closes on Nate’s
eyes”, and I was like ooh, what
does that mean?

00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:11.887
Rupert’s just bought West Ham
United!

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:13.013
No!

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:19.353
At the end of season two,
there’s a bit of a battleground
forming between

00:00:19.353 --> 00:00:22.731
Richmond and West Ham and that
battleground is the pitch!

00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:27.861
What Nate did, um, no one could
have seen coming.

00:00:27.903 --> 00:00:30.530
And, it feels like a huge
betrayal.

00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:32.241
Brett Goldstein:
I just felt sorry for him, like

00:00:32.407 --> 00:00:34.868
I was heartbroken for him at the
end of season two.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.288
Ted was always really good to
him, took him under his wing.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:39.998
Like, you know, stepped him up.

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:43.418
You made me feel like I was the
most important person in the
whole world.

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:44.419
I love it!

00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:46.880
Nate:
And then, you abandoned me.

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:51.551
Nate the betrayer, Nate the son
figure, I think Ted is all those
things.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.803
Jason Sudeikis:
I think we’re all, all those
things.

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:55.973
It's a really bold move by the
writers to take a character they
deliberately

00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:58.433
got everyone to root for and
then just take it away.

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:00.435
It’s always good to keep people
on their toes, isn't it?

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:02.688
Well, hey, next season
should be fun, right?

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:03.563
(Whistle blows)

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.565
(Crowd noise)

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:13.532
Two months have passed since
season two 

00:01:13.532 --> 00:01:16.326
and these characters are shaking
everything up.

00:01:17.411 --> 00:01:19.997
Reporter:
Regarding your old team AFC
Richmond, 

00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:24.543
any idea why everyone is
expecting them to finish
twentieth this season? 

00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:26.962
Probably because there’s no
twenty-first.

00:01:26.962 --> 00:01:28.297
(Reporters laugh)

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:32.342
We have to rebuild a family
because a family was broken.

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:36.138
If the team is a metaphor for a
society at large or a family,

00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:38.765
Jason Sudeikis:
we wanted to see how this family
dealt with it.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.309
Did you hear what Nathan was
saying about you?

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:40.934
Yes, ma’am.

00:01:40.976 --> 00:01:42.352
And are you planning on
addressing that?

00:01:42.728 --> 00:01:43.228
No, ma’am.

00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:46.440
I don’t think Rebecca can quite
believe that of all

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.777
the people that Nathan has gone
to, it’s F'ing Rupert.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:54.323
There he is, the Wonder Kid
himself.

00:01:54.406 --> 00:01:57.326
Rather than proving his worth to
the likes of Ted, who’s
obviously

00:01:57.326 --> 00:02:00.954
Nick Mohammed:
a force for good, he’s proving
it to Rupert who’s a force for bad.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:03.165
Nathan Shelley, you are a
killer.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.251
Good morning Viet—

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:07.252
(All)
Ted!

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:12.591
At the beginning, Ted will feel
a bit beholden to

00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:16.428
a flippant promise he made at
the end of season one to, uh,
win the whole thing.

00:02:16.511 --> 00:02:17.429
Woah! Did I really say that?

00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:21.266
Yes, you did! Over there before
you blasted half a liter of
Pellegrino in my face.

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:22.184
Oh, right.

00:02:22.184 --> 00:02:23.226
-Wait, what happened?

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:23.810
Let’s go!

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.439
I think Ted has the opportunity
this season to make things
better.

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:28.857
What do you think if
we signed Zava?

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:29.524
Ah!
-Oh!

00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:31.360
Second question. 
Who is Zava?

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:36.114
Zava is this once in a
generation footballer.

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:40.118
Am I to assume that you’re going
to pursue a notoriously
mercurial player

00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:43.121
Trent Crimm:
you can’t afford simply because
your ex-husband wants him?

00:02:44.748 --> 00:02:45.415
Yes.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:46.333
Love that.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:49.211
People are going to see in these
characters the growth 

00:02:49.211 --> 00:02:51.213
that they’ve always wanted to
see from season one.

00:02:52.214 --> 00:02:52.714
What are you doing?

00:02:52.714 --> 00:02:53.673
I was going to hug you!

00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:54.883
Well, you came at me too fast!

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.344
It's really interesting to watch
the team grow.

00:02:57.511 --> 00:02:59.805
Toheeb Jimoh:
Ultimately, that’s the story of
Ted Lasso, isn’t it?

00:03:00.055 --> 00:03:01.139
You are it. You are enough.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.643
Ted:
Expectations for us are as low
as a rattlesnake’s belly button, 

00:03:04.935 --> 00:03:07.938
but hey we got thirty-eight
chances to prove all them folks
wrong though, right?

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:11.733
It will be as fantastic as the
show has been, if not more so.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:12.943
How is it possible?

00:03:14.945 --> 00:03:15.487
Sport, 

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:16.905
Trent Crimm:
it’s quite the metaphor.

00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:19.533
♪♪

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:21.034
It also makes for a
heck of a nickname.

00:03:21.076 --> 00:03:25.080
♪♪

